### SE-F1 (S2) — first wheel event after stream: 151ms flush gap (threshold-grazer)
`wheel-scroll-transcript` cell: gap150@15008ms=151ms on the FIRST gap
of the wheel window, 3/3 reproducible runs (details:
/tmp/opencode/scanef2/e1-burst-details.log). 1ms over the clause's
>150ms rule with a ~117ms drive tick — logged per the threshold's
letter; user impact marginal (single 151ms hitch, scroll remains
fluid after). Suspect: lazy viewport work on first scroll. Fix-wave
target, not release-blocking.

### SE-F2 (S1) — PTY resize kills the exit chord: teardown wedge (deterministic)
Grow 80x24→100x30 (TIOCSWINSZ on the harness master, real SIGWINCH)
→ from that point the exit chord (\x03 + leader-q) NEVER tears the app
down; run-loop future does not return; app keeps rendering. Bisect
evidence (all under the same suite):
- resize present: wedge 5/5 runs (incl. settle 2500ms after restore,
  and grow-only with NO restore);
- resize skipped (EF2_SKIP=resize): 0 wedges;
- wheel skipped, resize kept: wedge (not wheel-related);
- **input stays ALIVE post-resize**: ctrl+p opens the palette
  (10.4KB emitted, `opened=true`), esc closes it, composer echoes
  'zz' (1455B) — everything works EXCEPT exit (probe log:
  /tmp/opencode/scanef2/e1-probe.log).
E9/B5-class (teardown residue + terminal-events family). User shape:
resize the window during a session → cannot quit with the chord (must
kill). Root-cause owned by the fix wave; repro = the committed test
with EF2 env knobs.

