### SE-F3 (S2) — eager boot-time snapshot git-init (ours-extra fs writes)
Our server initializes TWO bare git repos under
$HOME/.local/share/opencode-rust/snapshot/<projhash>/<snode>/ (config,
HEAD.lock, hooks, objects/pack, refs...) at BOOT, before any session
exists, in an EMPTY project dir. Ref has the Snapshot module
(core/src/snapshot.ts, capture/diff/restore) but writes NOTHING to it
in the same window (its usage sites are instance/session-scoped —
lazy). Boot-window fs churn ours-extra; disk-per-project footprint;
E2-boot-cost coupling. Fix-wave disposition: defer snapshot init to
first capture (lazy, ref-shaped).

